# ── hosted repos (the meta-repo control-plane convention) ───────────────────
# This workspace is a CONTROL PLANE: it may host the project's infra + service
# repos as INDEPENDENT, gitignored sibling subdirs (the meta-repo pattern), each
# tracked by .claude/foundry-project.json repos{} — NOT as git submodules. Anchor
# every hosted repo to the repo root with a leading slash so it is never tracked
# by the control plane, and add a matching repos{} entry. Runbook + the rationale
# (why siblings, not submodules): docs/SETUP.md 'Multi-repo control plane'.
#   /infra/          # example: your IaC repo (OpenTofu/Kubernetes) — uncomment when cloned
#   /<your-repo>/    # one line per hosted repo, root-anchored
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.foundry/security-audit.jsonl
.claude/dispatcher-mode.json
.claude/dispatcher-mode.json.lock
.claude/logs/
.claude/settings.local.json
.foundry/session-learnings/
.foundry/session-markers/
# FOUNDRY-RUNTIME-GITIGNORE-BEGIN (managed by scripts/foundry-apply-runtime-gitignore.sh -- do not edit by hand)
# .foundry/ runtime partitions are ignored by default; the designed-tracked set is re-included.
/.foundry/*
!/.foundry/README.md
!/.foundry/build-provenance.yaml
!/.foundry/stack-profile.lock
# FOUNDRY-RUNTIME-GITIGNORE-END (re-run the applier to converge; do not edit by hand)
